# OnOffMyPC Mobile — secrets & tokens inventory
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Copy:  cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill real values in .env  (NEVER commit .env — it is gitignored)
# 3. Rotate here; then mirror the values to where they are actually consumed
#    (see each section). This file is the single place to track them.
#
# NOTE: GitHub Actions does NOT read this file. CI secrets must be added at:
#   GitHub → onoffmypc-mobile → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
# This .env is your rotation/reference source + local signed-build config.
# To securely import the default files under android/ without printing secrets:
#   bash scripts/import-android-keystore.sh

# ── Payments are server-only ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do NOT add POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN, POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET, or product IDs here.
# Android and iOS request hosted checkout/portal links from the OnOffMyPC API;
# they never talk to Polar with privileged credentials. Configure all Polar
# values in the backend repository's .env instead.

# ── Release signing (local .env and GitHub Actions secrets) ─────────────────
# The same keystore/credentials are used by local signed builds and by CI.
# CI secret names are exactly: KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, KEY_ALIAS, KEY_PASSWORD.
# Password protecting the Android release keystore file.
KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
# Alias of the signing key inside the Android release keystore.
KEY_ALIAS=onoffmypc
# Password protecting that signing key; it may differ from the keystore password.
KEY_PASSWORD=
# Local path to the release JKS, resolved from this repository's root. An
# absolute path also works. The import script sets the default path to
# android/onoffmypc-release.jks. The file is gitignored and must remain private.
KEYSTORE_FILE=
# Base64 copy of the JKS for the GitHub secret ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64. Generate
# it with the import script above to avoid copy/paste corruption.
ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64=

# ── CI publish tokens (GitHub Actions repo secrets) ──────────────────────────
# release.yml (app-vX.Y.Z tag) publishes the APK to onoffmypc/onoffmypc-release.
# A missing/expired RELEASE_REPO_TOKEN is a common cause of a failed publish.
# Use a fine-grained PAT with Contents: write only on onoffmypc-release.
RELEASE_REPO_TOKEN=
# Single-line Google Play publishing service-account JSON consumed by play.yml.
# Leave blank when using only the direct APK distribution flow.
PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# ── Not secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# app/google-services.json is Firebase *client* config (not a secret).
# GitHub supplies GITHUB_TOKEN automatically to Actions; do not copy a personal
# token into this file for it. Prefer SSH remotes for private local dependencies.
